  "manual": {
    "notes": [
      "FABRICATED NOBLE FATHER (deep-chain audit, 2026-07-03): this is the real, documented Great Migration immigrant (b. Exeter 1590, m. Grace Townsend 1620, d. Lynn, MA 1666). His listed father, 'Sir John Winton \"Earl of Minorites\" Mansfield' (I182620325076), carries an invented peerage title — 'Minorites' refers to Franciscan friars (Order of Friars Minor), not a place or earldom, and no such creation exists in the Complete Peerage. This looks like an attempt to manufacture a noble ancestor by borrowing the prestige/surname of the real, documented Mansel family of Margam/Oxwich, Glamorgan (see I182620325139, Sir Rhys Mansel). Treat any claimed descent from the Welsh Mansels as unsupported legend; Robert Mansfield's actual English parentage is not established by sources found."
    ]
  }
